  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want « Expérimental » to be a single entry in Réglages that opens its own page, where every experimental option is listed with its switch, so that the main Réglages page stays clean and the experimental options are clearly set apart.\n\n### Today (#903)\n\n`ExperimentalSettingsSection` (`App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/ExperimentalSettingsView.swift:6-25`) adds an « Expérimental » **section** at the end of Réglages: one row per sub-menu (Messages, Composer…), each opening `ExperimentalThemeView`, with a footer.\n\n### Wanted (operator, 2026-11-16)\n\n- Réglages shows **one row « Expérimental »**, preceded by a **warning symbol**: monochrome, in the text colour (e.g. SF Symbol `exclamationmark.triangle`, `.foregroundStyle(.primary)`, not an emoji, not tinted).\n- That row opens a **new settings page « Expérimental »** listing the experimental options to switch on or off. Keep the sub-menus as sections of that page (Messages, Composer, Listes, Chargement des images…), with each option's switch and its ⓘ. The footer « Options en cours de mise au point, désactivées par défaut. » moves to that page.\n- The row is hidden when no option is listed, as today.\n- VoiceOver reads « Expérimental »; the symbol is decorative.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Réglages has one « Expérimental » row with the monochrome warning symbol; tapping it opens the page with every listed option.\n- [ ] Every option keeps its storage key: no setting is lost.\n- [ ] A test fails without the change: the Réglages section exposes one navigation row; the page lists all listed features grouped by theme.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
